{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And it shall be</b> — <b>not shall it be</b>: serves on account of another instance." "<b>And the word יקרות</b> — is an adjective, and the modified noun is עבות. Thus: <b>not shall there be light, and not shall there be</b> עבות <b>יקרות</b>." "<b>And קפאון</b> — a heavy thing, like <b>not day and not night</b>."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The Hebrew quotes the constructive/absolute forms of היה; the argument appears truncated and the reference of 'another instance' is left cryptic.", 1 "Ibn Ezra parses יקרות as modifying עבות rather than standing independently.", 2 "Possibly read as interpreting קרירות (coldness/congealment) as 'heaviness'; the word קפאון may be Ibn Ezra's own lexical label for the atmospheric condition described."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:02.843980596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}